# Phase 3 remoting transport execution log

- Date/session: 2026-09-26 UTC, `20260926T092647Z`.
- Scope: continue Phase 3 only; no Phase 4 work. Read both Phase 3 plans completely; plans left unchanged. Oracle remains Java RocketMQ 5.5.1; Phase 19 live validation stays pending.
- Java source evidence: `NettyRemotingClient.invokeOneway` calls `getAndCreateChannelAsync(addr)` before return and handles future completion asynchronously. Rust's previous plain `tokio::spawn(connection(...))` did not guarantee any poll before return.
- Change: oneway now polls the acquire future exactly once synchronously, then transfers a pending future into an owned Tokio task; a separate owned operation task awaits its result. No connect completion, admission or write is awaited. Synchronous Rust address parsing reports invalid syntax through the already-ready result future; post-return TCP/connect/admission/write errors remain unobservable.
- Tests: added `oneway_connection_acquisition_enters_connect_before_return` (checks registered single-flight gate is held before return), `spawned_connection_future_is_polled_before_return`, and integration regression `p3_oneway_reports_invalid_address_to_returned_result`. The new invalid-address test failed on the old implementation (the error was lost in the background task), then passed after the targeted fix. Existing `p3_oneway_starts_connection_acquisition_at_call_time` remains passing.
- Documentation: updated Java compatibility status and Phase 3 bidirectional inventory for the exact start boundary and remaining failure visibility. No plan edits.
